<title>USA: AMEX closes higher, Canyon Resources rises.</title>
<headline>AMEX closes higher, Canyon Resources rises.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prices on the American Stock Exchange closed higher in moderate trading with Canyon Resources Corp gaining more than 10 percent on Friday.</p>
<p>The Amex Composite index closed at 573.78, up 2.83 or 0.5 percent. The average price per share was up six cents.</p>
<p>More stocks rose than fell, with a 307 to 215 ratio. There were 175 unchanged stocks.</p>
<p>Preliminary volume was 17,835,670, compared with 20,822,085 on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Canyon Resources closed up 5/16 to 2-15/16 after an upgrade by Alex. Brown.</p>
<p>(Prices official as of 1630 EST/2130 GMT)</p>
<p>((-- Wall Street desk, 212-859-1730))</p>
